// Title: Suspicious Service Binary Directory
// Sigma ID: 883faa95-175a-4e22-8181-e5761aeb373c
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-03-09 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1202
// Description: Detects a service binary running in a suspicious directory
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://blog.truesec.com/2021/03/07/exchange-zero-day-proxylogon-and-hafnium/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_service_dir.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "\\Users\\Public\\" or FolderPath contains "\\$Recycle.bin" or FolderPath contains "\\Users\\All Users\\" or FolderPath contains "\\Users\\Default\\" or FolderPath contains "\\Users\\Contacts\\" or FolderPath contains "\\Users\\Searches\\" or FolderPath contains "C:\\Perflogs\\" or FolderPath contains "\\config\\systemprofile\\" or FolderPath contains "\\Windows\\Fonts\\" or FolderPath contains "\\Windows\\IME\\" or FolderPath contains "\\Windows\\addins\\") and (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\services.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\svchost.exe")
